From ff5511956329c52b772c991584804f7ee0c3a76e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Crowe <michael@crowelogic.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 23:54:50 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Sense: the Crowe Sense node as a workbench panel, read live

A new panel type "sense" beside Projects, wired the same way at every
seam: TabKey/PanelTabKey/PANEL_TABS/TAB_ORDER/TAB_LABELS, PanelType and
FOCUS_EXISTING_ON_ADD, panel-graph titles, Workspace PANEL_LABELS and
the PanelContent switch, the LeftRail workbench entry (IconSense), the
App typeMap, and the command palette.

src/config/sense.ts holds the source (off | direct | cloud) in
localStorage the way config/farm.ts does; senseEndpoint() maps the
contract paths (crowe-sense/contracts/telemetry-v1.md) onto either the
node's own API or the relay's /v1/nodes/<node> mount. src/lib/sense-client
does the typed reads with a 10 s timeout, the Crowe ID bearer in cloud
mode, and every failure reduced to the contract's {error, detail} pair.

SenseTab renders GET /api/data?hours=6: a tile row per grow zone
(temperature, humidity, CO2, VPD, then fruiting score by band, dew
point, light), three inline-SVG sparklines, a Flow hood section, a
Controller section, a settings row that persists and refetches, and a
15 s refresh while mounted. Off shows an empty state, never a demo;
a failed read shows the detail text. Tokens only, square corners,
hair-top bevel, card shadow.

Tests: SenseTab.test.tsx, 8 cases (direct render incl. sparklines and
sections, empty when off, unreachable, contract 404 pair, save and
refetch, senseEndpoint both modes and refusals).
